  "score": "Squared Mahalanobis distance of the real shape from the Gaussian fit of a population at the same c. The ensemble population is the pool of samples_per_model prior draws from every member. The oracle population is n_true fresh draws from the true conditional.",
  "regularisation": {
    "rule": "cov + noise_std**2 * I before the Mahalanobis solve",
    "noise_std": 0.01,
    "noise_var": 0.0001,
    "tuned_on_test": false,
    "tuned_on_calibration_coverage": false,
    "why": "noise_std is the synthetic coordinate noise. Adding its variance on the diagonal stops near-zero eigenvalues of a collapsed covariance from dominating the score, and it does not inflate the trace up to the true conditional trace. The value is part of the data definition. Coverage was not used to pick it. The naive chi-square quantile still uses 128 degrees of freedom; the floor means that quantile is not exact even for a correct Gaussian.",
